# STI—Set Interrupt Flag -- override
# As CLI (no VME/PVI): IF := 1 where CLI would clear it, else #GP(0). "If
# IF = 0, maskable hardware interrupts remain inhibited on the instruction
# boundary following an execution of STI" (Description): InhibitInterrupts.
@operation
IF CR0.PE = 1 AND RFLAGS.VM = 0 AND CPL > IOPL THEN #GP(0); FI;
IF CR0.PE = 1 AND RFLAGS.VM = 1 AND IOPL != 3 THEN #GP(0); FI;
IF INTF = 0 THEN InhibitInterrupts; FI;
SetFlag(INTF, 1);
